# Stage 5 — PHP filters and actions, JS hooks, and jQuery event names.
#
# These are the plugin's public surface. Renaming them is a deliberate break,
# taken on the understanding that this build is for new sites: any snippet in
# functions.php, any custom JS bound to gform_post_render, and any third-party
# integration written against the old names stops firing, silently and with no
# error. The eight add-ons in this repo are checked and use none of them.
#
# Both sides always move together — the add_filter and the apply_filters, the
# gform.addAction and the gform.doAction, the .on() and the .trigger() — so
# nothing inside this tree is left listening for a name that is no longer
# fired.

